## 1. Source of truth

| Layer                 | Path                                       |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Reusable kit          | `{{KIT_ROOT}}/` (read-only at runtime)     |
| Project harness       | `.harness/` (project-owned)                |
| Project knowledge     | `docs/` (project-owned)                    |
| Current project state | `docs/00-project-control/current-state.yml`|
| Active work pointer   | `docs/00-project-control/active-work.md`   |

Rule: **AI never modifies `{{KIT_ROOT}}/`.** Improvements to the kit go
through `propose-harness-improvement` (see `.harness/commands.yml`).

---

## 2. Reading order at session start

1. `CLEAN_STATE_CHECKLIST.md` (start-of-session block)
2. `docs/00-project-control/current-state.yml`
3. `docs/00-project-control/active-work.md`
4. The active task file referenced from `current-state.yml`
5. `.harness/gates.yml` rules relevant to current phase
6. `.harness/quality.yml` (anti-fiction, documentation, memory rules)

If `current-state.yml.current.lifecycle_status` is `initialized` and
`active_task` is null, the only allowed next action is to run
`bootstrap-project-context`.

