## 4. End of session

**Mandatory command: `end-session`.** Before reporting a session as done,
every AI worker must execute the `end-session` contract in
`.harness/commands.yml`. This applies to documentation, analysis, planning,
implementation, review, and transition sessions; it is not limited to a
runtime agent execution.

Do not report completion until all applicable records are reconciled:

- Always update `docs/00-project-control/logs/progress-log.md` with the
  date, completed work, material blockers/decisions, and next governed action.
- Always update `docs/04-delivery/session-handoffs/latest-session.md` with
  an actionable continuation handoff.
- When task, sprint, branch, feature, or next action changes, reconcile
  `current-state.yml`, `active-work.md`, `project-status.md`, and
  `product-progress.md`.
- When a question, decision, risk, document registration, or maturity changes,
  reconcile its authoritative register and applicable rendered view.
- Append to `transition-log.md` only after an explicit, governed lifecycle
  confirmation. A transition is never required for the progress log or latest
  session handoff.

For an agent execution, both the progress log and latest-session handoff must
cite the exact execution ID before `close-session` may return it to a gate.

